        "id": "p9-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate $y$ using Pythagoras’ theorem.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=24\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "The perpendicular height bisects the 20 cm base because the triangle is isosceles.\n$$\\begin{align*}y^2+10^2&=26^2\\\\y^2&=676-100=576\\\\y&=\\sqrt{576}=24\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, show the volume is approximately $10\\,583\\text{ cm}^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$V=14\\,400-1215\\pi\\approx10\\,583\\text{ cm}^3$.",
          "worked": "The hole has radius $9\\div2=4.5\\text{ cm}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}V_{\\text{prism}}&=\\left(\\frac12\\times20\\times24\\right)\\times60=14\\,400\\text{ cm}^3\\\\V_{\\text{hole}}&=\\pi(4.5)^2\\times60=1215\\pi\\text{ cm}^3\\\\V&=14\\,400-1215\\pi\\text{ cm}^3\\\\V&\\approx10\\,583\\text{ cm}^3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ],
